	(text "SYNCHRONOUS DEMOD - AD831 mixer + 2-pole RC LPF  |  \n(Phase reference is now a dedicated AD9833 - see RefDDS_AD9833 block.)\nLO1_REF is the phase-set reference tone at Omega from the reference DDS (DDS3) in Laser_Control; \ndemod phase is set DIGITALLY via that DDS phase register (no analog all-pass).\nMixer U821=AD831 (generic 6-pin: 1=RF 2=LO 3=IF 4=V+ 5=V- 6=GND -> REMAP to real AD831). \nRF from TIA1_OUT via C821 DC-block. AD633 is the fallback if Omega<=~1MHz.\nPost-mix 2-pole RC LPF (R823/C822/R824/C823 = 3.3k/1n) fc~48kHz: rejects the 2*Omega product (4-5MHz), \npasses baseband error ERR1 to the PI servo and Teensy monitor.\nConnectivity is by coincident net-name LABELS at pin tips. \n\nswap AD831 generic symbol for the real part.  Channel 2 = LO2_REF / TIA2_OUT / ERR2."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
